                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98a685ff-ec5e-3be9-8b87-26974ff4e374",
                        "entry_id": "5aae8375-d056-3be8-9a4d-d51885984864",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An abnormal protrusion of the uveal tissue through the eyeball."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90c3300e-d786-4f98-be81-d6a38e3c7b5f",
                                "sense_id": "98a685ff-ec5e-3be9-8b87-26974ff4e374",
                                "text": "Staphyloma is that disease of the eyeball, in which the cornea loses its natural transparency, rises above the level of the eye, and successively even projects beyond the eyelids […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebfc6192-df02-4827-97c8-0bce4674e268",
                                "sense_id": "98a685ff-ec5e-3be9-8b87-26974ff4e374",
                                "text": "One of the forms of staphyloma, which is regarded as in no degree malignant, appears to be essentially composed of a collection of cysts; and, as far as I can judge from mere description, having never had an opportunity of examining a case of the kind myself, is connected with that form of adventitious serous membrane with which we are now occupied."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18aa9385-fedc-49ff-9b3d-1da2806b9e51",
                                "sense_id": "98a685ff-ec5e-3be9-8b87-26974ff4e374",
                                "text": "Abscission of the staphyloma should never be performed where there is reason to suspect pre-existing disease of the choroid or retina, as deep haemorrhage is likely to follow the removal of the front of the globe, which may necessitate the rest of the eye."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
